    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "grieving doesn't fix the math though. the time is gone and it's never coming back. i just feel like i'm pouring more energy into a machine that's broken. it's like when you're in a game and you realize the save file is corrupted and everything you did was for nothing, you don't keep playing for another twenty years just to see the error message. you just close the game and walk away. why should i keep grinding for a life that's already a total loss?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
